# EaglercraftX 1.8.8 loads (cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2, T-666): the offline JavaScript build, served from the host's
# cache (tools/host/eaglercraft/eaglercraft-fetch.py; port 8099), within the bound written in the kit before the round:
# 180 s from the start of the load to the title screen. What a person does on the way, read in the first rounds
# (docs/rounds/t666-2026-11-18): the client extracts its assets in one script task of 60-120 s, past the engine's
# 60 s guard (the owner keeps it, 2026-11-19), so the slow-script dialog asks once or twice and Continue is tapped
# each time (`wait rect-ok`, which says how many); with the
# UA's Tablet token (the owner, 2026-11-19) the client takes the device for a tablet and shows its "Mobile Browser
# Detected" panel, whose "Launch EaglercraftX" is tapped (in desktop mode it waited for a key a touch screen cannot
# press). The title screen is read by eye from the kept picture until its reference picture exists (host cache only:
# it carries Mojang's art); the page's own clock (performance.now()) says when it came.
id: eagler-load-188
section: Eaglercraft
item: EaglercraftX 1.8.8 (the offline build, from the host) reaches its title screen within 180 s: Continue on the slow-script dialog its extraction brings, Launch on its tablet panel
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8099/eaglerx-1.8.8/unpacked/eaglercraft1-8.html
kit: cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2
wait rect-ok 'sel:._eaglercraftX_mobile_launch_client' 420
shoot launch
probe launch-at '(function(){return "launch panel at "+Math.round(performance.now()/1000)+" s; ua tablet "+/tablet/i.test(navigator.userAgent);})()'
tap 'sel:._eaglercraftX_mobile_launch_client'
wait gone 'sel:._eaglercraftX_mobile_launch_client' 10
wait quiet 'jihad-never-logged' 30
shoot after-launch
wait quiet 'jihad-never-logged' 30
shoot after-launch-60
probe title-at '(function(){var c=document.querySelectorAll("canvas"),s=[];for(var i=0;i<c.length;i++){s.push(c[i].width+"x"+c[i].height);}return "at "+Math.round(performance.now()/1000)+" s, canvases "+c.length+" ["+s.join(",")+"]";})()'
show-log 'rror\|WebGL\|webgl\|memory guard\|OOM'
